WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.386
Create a benchmark that represents the intended workload and can be repeated.

00:00:05.386 --> 00:00:11.969
Record the exact model, quantization, runtime, backend, settings, prompt, requested output length, and hardware state.

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:20.546
Include one short interactive prompt, one normal task, and one stress case with longer context if the workflow needs it.

00:00:20.546 --> 00:00:25.932
Keep generation settings fixed so sampling variation does not obscure system changes.

00:00:25.932 --> 00:00:33.312
Measure model load time, time to first token, prompt-processing rate, generation tokens per second, and end-to-end completion.

00:00:33.312 --> 00:00:41.890
Track peak VRAM, system RAM, GPU and CPU utilization, disk activity, temperature, clock speed, fan behavior, and power where available.

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:48.872
A performance improvement that raises errors, throttling, or output defects must be evaluated as a tradeoff.

00:00:48.872 --> 00:00:50.667
Run several trials.

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:58.446
The first run may include model loading and cold caches, while later runs may benefit from retained data.

00:00:58.446 --> 00:01:03.034
Long sessions reveal thermal behavior that a ten-second benchmark misses.

00:01:03.034 --> 00:01:09.218
Report median or typical results and note outliers instead of selecting the best number.

00:01:09.218 --> 00:01:16.998
Test both an idle machine and the normal desktop environment if background applications are part of actual use.

00:01:16.998 --> 00:01:23.181
Change one variable at a time and log the result in a small table.

00:01:23.181 --> 00:01:28.567
Compare not only percentages but whether the difference is noticeable and repeatable.

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:33.953
After synthetic tuning, return to real tasks and assess quality and usability.

00:01:33.953 --> 00:01:42.132
The purpose of a benchmark is to support a decision: keep the change, reject it, or investigate a bottleneck.

00:01:42.132 --> 00:01:46.320
It is not a score to maximize without context.
